\description{
A regex lookup mapping cardiac ablation brand names as they appear in MAUDE's
\code{device_brand_name} field onto a platform, an energy modality, and the entity
that makes it. Maintained as two files --
\code{data-raw/maude-entities/ablation-patterns.csv}, one brand alias per row, and
\code{ablation-platforms.csv}, one platform per row -- joined at build time and
applied by \code{\link[=normalize_maude_ablation]{normalize_maude_ablation()}}.
}
\details{
It exists because product code does not determine modality: \code{OAE} covers
cryoablation and radiofrequency alike, and a rule that resolves it from the
product code alone will place cryoballoon, pulsed-field, and laser devices in
a radiofrequency arm.

Two things it is careful about. Substring matching on \code{"arctic"} is not a
cryoablation signal, since \code{"ARCTIC SUN"} is a targeted temperature
management console; the pattern is \code{"ARCTIC FRONT"}. And mapping, access, and
irrigation devices share the ablation product codes, so \code{PENTARAY},
\code{OCTARAY}, \code{FARADRIVE}, \code{RHYTHMIA}, \code{ENSITE} and others are in the table with
a \code{modality} of \code{NA} rather than being swept into whichever arm their product
code implies.

The \code{entity} column names the maker, never the corporate parent, so the table
does not have to be edited when a company is acquired. Pass it to
\code{\link[=resolve_maude_owner]{resolve_maude_owner()}} with a date for the parent.

Coverage is measured on each rebuild and travels with the data:
\code{attr(maude_ablation_index, "coverage")}, with the full report in
\code{data-raw/maude-entities/coverage.md}.
